* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
artifacts/evidence/rcl-205/** binary -eol

# Storage fidelity for hash-bound evidence. Every path below has its sha256
# declared in a manifest, an approval record, or the erratum, and those hashes
# are computed over the bytes on disk. Git must store exactly those bytes, or a
# fresh checkout cannot reproduce a declared hash. See evidence discipline
# rule 11 and corpus/ERRATUM_001_p1-frozen-001.md revision 3.
# Pure evidence artifacts. Opaque bytes: their changes surface as hash changes,
# not as textual diffs. cr-at-eol stops the whitespace checker reading the CR of
# a CRLF line ending as trailing whitespace on files we deliberately keep byte
# faithful.
artifacts/evidence/** -text -diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
corpus/generated/** -text -diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
corpus/FROZEN_CONFIG.json -text -diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
corpus/PRIVACY_CORPUS_MANIFEST.json -text -diff whitespace=cr-at-eol
corpus/ARM_DECLARATION.json -text -diff whitespace=cr-at-eol

# Hash-bound code and data. Byte faithful for the same reason, but reviewers
# legitimately read these as diffs, so they keep textual diff and take the
# whitespace rule alone.
corpus/generator.py -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
corpus/data/gazetteers.json -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
scripts/derive_corrected_view.py -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
